From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 09:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(soup): reinstate the Garden/XR entry chip in the sessions toolbar

RE-CUT 2026-11-24 against composed tip 45abeaa2b. The original (dated
2026-11-19) stopped applying when the toolbarExtras region moved, and a
failed `apply -3` leaves partial debris in the remat worktree, so a stale
heal is worse than none.

The reason this must stay a heal, unchanged from the original: upstream moved
the sessions header into <SessionList renderHeader>, so the layer merge takes
the base for that region and the chip loses its home. toolbarExtras sits
OUTSIDE the conflict region — git treats it as context, rerere replays only
conflicted regions, so a hand edit there is silently dropped by the next
compose, and full-recipe mode recomposes from the base every run.

Found unrendered on the promoted tip: GardenXrEntryChip was imported at
router.tsx:109 and rendered NOWHERE, so the Garden/XR entry point did not
exist in the UI. Typecheck is happy with an unused import and no test asserts
the toolbar's contents, so nothing reported it. A fail-closed check now does:
verify-sessionlist-bindings.mjs rejects an entry-point component that
router.tsx imports but never renders.
diff --git a/web/src/router.tsx b/web/src/router.tsx
index 6c9a4981a..4587915ef 100644
--- a/web/src/router.tsx
+++ b/web/src/router.tsx
@@ -1149,6 +1149,19 @@ function SessionsPage() {
                         // browse 8, overseer 9, import 10 (#2039).
                         renderHeader={false}
                         toolbarExtras={[
+                            {
+                                // Garden/XR entry (fork). It used to sit inline beside
+                                // the session count in this file; upstream moved that
+                                // header into <SessionList renderHeader>, so the chip
+                                // belongs in the toolbar rather than in a header this
+                                // file no longer renders. Without this entry the
+                                // component is imported here and rendered NOWHERE —
+                                // the entry point is simply unreachable, which is the
+                                // state the composed tip was in.
+                                id: 'garden-xr',
+                                keep: 4,
+                                node: <GardenXrEntryChip />
+                            },
                             {
                                 id: 'settings',
                                 keep: 6,
-- 
